  "chunks": [
    {
      "scene_id": "s01-negotiation",
      "asset_id": "narr-s01-negotiation",
      "route": "tts",
      "path": "narration/s01-negotiation/a3fe53102a06ea3f.wav",
      "sha256": "e96dbde41516f8475661afe58ed58663ee4a6047ec18181389056be2730ded86",
      "fingerprint": "a3fe53102a06ea3fede3dfcd0eab63b54b9efcd8c35b4396d18982a95c9b5aca",
      "cached": false,
      "duration_seconds": 59.04,
      "sample_rate": 48000,
      "channels": 1,
      "integrated_lufs": -20.1,
      "true_peak_dbtp": -1.7,
      "leading_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "trailing_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Have you ever met someone who seems to break every rule…",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.98
        },
        {
          "text": "and wins anyway?",
          "start": 3.48,
          "end": 4.706
        },
        {
          "text": "Here's the situation. For three years, you've believed one thing.",
          "start": 5.656,
          "end": 9.472
        },
        {
          "text": "Hard work wins.",
          "start": 10.202,
          "end": 11.118
        },
        {
          "text": "So you gave up your weekends.",
          "start": 12.218,
          "end": 14.014
        },
        {
          "text": "You said no to rest.",
          "start": 14.394,
          "end": 15.635
        },
        {
          "text": "You watched other people enjoy the things you kept putting off.",
          "start": 16.135,
          "end": 19.545
        },
        {
          "text": "And it felt worth it…",
          "start": 19.995,
          "end": 21.241
        },
        {
          "text": "because you believed.",
          "start": 21.741,
          "end": 23.308
        },
        {
          "text": "Then you meet someone. They work fewer hours.",
          "start": 24.158,
          "end": 26.646
        },
        {
          "text": "They protect their evenings. And they earn more than you.",
          "start": 26.976,
          "end": 30.116
        },
        {
          "text": "Now you're holding two ideas that don't fit together.",
          "start": 31.116,
          "end": 33.975
        },
        {
          "text": "You could rethink what success really takes.",
          "start": 34.925,
          "end": 37.326
        },
        {
          "text": "Or…",
          "start": 38.226,
          "end": 38.652
        },
        {
          "text": "you could decide they just got lucky.",
          "start": 39.152,
          "end": 41.301
        },
        {
          "text": "That it won't last. That they must know someone.",
          "start": 41.721,
          "end": 44.285
        },
        {
          "text": "Notice what just happened. Instead of changing your understanding of the world, you found a way to preserve it.",
          "start": 45.385,
          "end": 51.239
        },
        {
          "text": "And here's the strange part.",
          "start": 52.089,
          "end": 53.562
        },
        {
          "text": "From the inside, it doesn't feel like an excuse.",
          "start": 54.182,
          "end": 56.989
        },
        {
          "text": "It feels like logic.",
          "start": 57.769,
          "end": 59.024
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "s02-theory",
      "asset_id": "narr-s02-theory",
      "route": "tts",
      "path": "narration/s02-theory/00d40cea3868125c.wav",
      "sha256": "731666d32fe1da66e3f6f7f5d794f8be70824bbae2718bf8d2dcf6946d817c0d",
      "fingerprint": "00d40cea3868125c7ac52441b09ba0421ed7bc3b2b922ee63cd0db55e5f187c0",
      "cached": false,
      "duration_seconds": 56.105,
      "sample_rate": 48000,
      "channels": 1,
      "integrated_lufs": -20.1,
      "true_peak_dbtp": -1.6,
      "leading_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "trailing_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Psychology has a name for that feeling.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.38
        },
        {
          "text": "In 1957, a social psychologist named Leon Festinger called it cognitive dissonance.",
          "start": 3.33,
          "end": 8.855
        },
        {
          "text": "The idea is simple. When two things you believe don't fit together…",
          "start": 9.955,
          "end": 14.018
        },
        {
          "text": "or when what you do doesn't fit what you believe…",
          "start": 14.518,
          "end": 17.072
        },
        {
          "text": "it feels uncomfortable. And you want that feeling gone.",
          "start": 17.572,
          "end": 20.827
        },
        {
          "text": "Take a smoker. They know smoking is harmful.",
          "start": 21.677,
          "end": 24.181
        },
        {
          "text": "And they still smoke.",
          "start": 25.081,
          "end": 26.083
        },
        {
          "text": "So what do they do?",
          "start": 27.083,
          "end": 28.303
        },
        {
          "text": "They could quit. They could admit the habit clashes with their health.",
          "start": 28.873,
          "end": 32.316
        },
        {
          "text": "Or they could tell themselves…",
          "start": 32.866,
          "end": 34.677
        },
        {
          "text": "I don't smoke enough for it to matter.",
          "start": 35.177,
          "end": 37.117
        },
        {
          "text": "That's the key. Changing your mind is only one way out.",
          "start": 38.067,
          "end": 41.196
        },
        {
          "text": "You can change what you do.",
          "start": 41.576,
          "end": 43.055
        },
        {
          "text": "You can reinterpret the evidence.",
          "start": 43.555,
          "end": 45.558
        },
        {
          "text": "Or you can add a new story that makes the conflict feel smaller.",
          "start": 46.008,
          "end": 49.472
        },
        {
          "text": "Which way you go depends on the situation…",
          "start": 50.572,
          "end": 53.201
        },
        {
          "text": "and on how much that belief matters to you.",
          "start": 53.701,
          "end": 56.086
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "s03-experiment",
      "asset_id": "narr-s03-experiment",
      "route": "tts",
      "path": "narration/s03-experiment/edfa56eec5871a5a.wav",
      "sha256": "0f27cb8066059a95cc8631d62789c428c64961f1f269eb0c85c5791373c2d03c",
      "fingerprint": "edfa56eec5871a5add72c188d618d35e3a32cb8d4a58b5649058439b691837d4",
      "cached": true,
      "duration_seconds": 74.957,
      "sample_rate": 48000,
      "channels": 1,
      "integrated_lufs": -20.1,
      "true_peak_dbtp": -1.5,
      "leading_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "trailing_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Two years later, Festinger and a colleague, James Carl-smith, published an experiment that still surprises people.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 6.35
        },
        {
          "text": "Students came into a lab and spent about an hour on deliberately boring tasks.",
          "start": 7.3,
          "end": 11.895
        },
        {
          "text": "Like turning pegs on a board…",
          "start": 12.445,
          "end": 14.137
        },
        {
          "text": "a quarter turn at a time.",
          "start": 14.637,
          "end": 16.379
        },
        {
          "text": "Then came the twist. Some of them were asked to tell the next student that it had all been enjoyable.",
          "start": 17.479,
          "end": 23.081
        },
        {
          "text": "Some were paid one dollar to say it.",
          "start": 23.461,
          "end": 25.572
        },
        {
          "text": "Others were paid twenty. And a control group was never asked at all.",
          "start": 26.072,
          "end": 30.318
        },
        {
          "text": "Afterwards, everyone rated how enjoyable the tasks really were.",
          "start": 31.168,
          "end": 34.956
        },
        {
          "text": "You'd expect the twenty dollar group to like it more.",
          "start": 35.956,
          "end": 38.723
        },
        {
          "text": "They were paid more. But the opposite happened.",
          "start": 39.273,
          "end": 41.602
        },
        {
          "text": "The one dollar group rated the tasks clearly higher.",
          "start": 42.552,
          "end": 45.554
        },
        {
          "text": "The twenty dollar group landed close to the control group.",
          "start": 46.174,
          "end": 49.386
        },
        {
          "text": "Why?",
          "start": 50.486,
          "end": 50.845
        },
        {
          "text": "Twenty dollars was reason enough to say something you didn't believe.",
          "start": 51.495,
          "end": 55.14
        },
        {
          "text": "One dollar wasn't. So the easier way to make it fit…",
          "start": 55.59,
          "end": 58.838
        },
        {
          "text": "was to decide the tasks hadn't been that bad.",
          "start": 59.338,
          "end": 61.719
        },
        {
          "text": "It doesn't prove we always rewrite our beliefs to match our actions.",
          "start": 62.569,
          "end": 66.281
        },
        {
          "text": "But it shows something real.",
          "start": 66.611,
          "end": 68.288
        },
        {
          "text": "What we do can shape what we believe…",
          "start": 68.908,
          "end": 71.122
        },
        {
          "text": "especially when we can't easily justify it to ourselves.",
          "start": 71.622,
          "end": 74.94
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "s04-identity",
      "asset_id": "narr-s04-identity",
      "route": "tts",
      "path": "narration/s04-identity/cdac14e923fff454.wav",
      "sha256": "149c891daf50242a668296c04d5d73c9ebe6321b400a238afd1f34204b009ea3",
      "fingerprint": "cdac14e923fff454ea2bb5354e5a49358d21e1ba40157ce28f029d17f85d937f",
      "cached": true,
      "duration_seconds": 58.203,
      "sample_rate": 48000,
      "channels": 1,
      "integrated_lufs": -20.0,
      "true_peak_dbtp": -2.5,
      "leading_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "trailing_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "But not every contradiction hurts the same.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.598
        },
        {
          "text": "Find out you got a film's release year wrong?",
          "start": 3.548,
          "end": 6.021
        },
        {
          "text": "You won't lose sleep. Find out your politics rest on a false assumption…",
          "start": 6.721,
          "end": 10.953
        },
        {
          "text": "that's different.",
          "start": 11.453,
          "end": 12.407
        },
        {
          "text": "The difference is what the belief is carrying.",
          "start": 13.507,
          "end": 15.968
        },
        {
          "text": "Some beliefs are just information.",
          "start": 16.348,
          "end": 18.438
        },
        {
          "text": "Others are tied to who you are.",
          "start": 18.938,
          "end": 20.91
        },
        {
          "text": "Your relationships. The choices you've already made.",
          "start": 21.36,
          "end": 24.178
        },
        {
          "text": "Think about the career you spent years building.",
          "start": 25.028,
          "end": 27.495
        },
        {
          "text": "The relationship you defended to your friends.",
          "start": 28.045,
          "end": 30.681
        },
        {
          "text": "The beliefs you grew up with…",
          "start": 31.011,
          "end": 32.75
        },
        {
          "text": "shared with people you love.",
          "start": 33.25,
          "end": 34.984
        },
        {
          "text": "Changing your mind about any of these isn't just fixing a fact.",
          "start": 35.984,
          "end": 39.644
        },
        {
          "text": "It can mean admitting a sacrifice was unnecessary.",
          "start": 40.144,
          "end": 43.314
        },
        {
          "text": "Or that a decision was wrong.",
          "start": 43.764,
          "end": 45.678
        },
        {
          "text": "That's why an argument that looks simple from the outside can feel so threatening from the inside.",
          "start": 46.628,
          "end": 52.045
        },
        {
          "text": "The contradiction is carrying more than information.",
          "start": 52.595,
          "end": 55.541
        },
        {
          "text": "It is carrying consequences.",
          "start": 56.271,
          "end": 58.185
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "s05-motivated",
      "asset_id": "narr-s05-motivated",
      "route": "tts",
      "path": "narration/s05-motivated/540f7ff8a2b50549.wav",
      "sha256": "6a3d63884b653c76a39d67cc479d58dd7dbeb4509bb481791240cef7fd64f009",
      "fingerprint": "540f7ff8a2b505498452b1fa61d7b3c542ae40eecd457c14a93898707f0bbc96",
      "cached": true,
      "duration_seconds": 66.341,
      "sample_rate": 48000,
      "channels": 1,
      "integrated_lufs": -20.0,
      "true_peak_dbtp": -1.7,
      "leading_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "trailing_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "There's a second idea that helps here.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 2.16
        },
        {
          "text": "It's called motivated reasoning.",
          "start": 2.98,
          "end": 4.956
        },
        {
          "text": "It's the way our goals and commitments shape how we judge information.",
          "start": 5.906,
          "end": 9.844
        },
        {
          "text": "Picture two smart people reading the same study.",
          "start": 10.944,
          "end": 13.734
        },
        {
          "text": "One finds it supports what they already believe.",
          "start": 14.354,
          "end": 17.061
        },
        {
          "text": "So they notice the solid methods…",
          "start": 17.441,
          "end": 19.588
        },
        {
          "text": "and the clear results. The other finds it challenges them.",
          "start": 20.088,
          "end": 23.291
        },
        {
          "text": "So they notice the limitations…",
          "start": 23.741,
          "end": 25.868
        },
        {
          "text": "and everything that could be wrong.",
          "start": 26.368,
          "end": 28.321
        },
        {
          "text": "Now, being critical is good science.",
          "start": 29.171,
          "end": 31.06
        },
        {
          "text": "The problem is when the standard changes…",
          "start": 31.39,
          "end": 33.807
        },
        {
          "text": "depending on whether we like the answer.",
          "start": 34.307,
          "end": 36.585
        },
        {
          "text": "But here's the hopeful part.",
          "start": 37.585,
          "end": 39.277
        },
        {
          "text": "In 2019, the psychologist Stephanie Anglin reported four studies.",
          "start": 39.777,
          "end": 43.542
        },
        {
          "text": "And people often did change their beliefs when the evidence was clear.",
          "start": 43.992,
          "end": 47.906
        },
        {
          "text": "Even on religion, politics, and capital punishment.",
          "start": 48.326,
          "end": 51.441
        },
        {
          "text": "Bias showed up sometimes…",
          "start": 52.391,
          "end": 54.181
        },
        {
          "text": "but not always.",
          "start": 54.681,
          "end": 55.636
        },
        {
          "text": "So the real question isn't whether people are rational.",
          "start": 56.586,
          "end": 59.738
        },
        {
          "text": "It's this. When do we judge evidence on its merits…",
          "start": 60.118,
          "end": 62.971
        },
        {
          "text": "and when do we judge it by whether we want it to be true?",
          "start": 63.471,
          "end": 66.322
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "s06-brain",
      "asset_id": "narr-s06-brain",
      "route": "tts",
      "path": "narration/s06-brain/62f120370bd53e99.wav",
      "sha256": "510e6aab8dd13e798074c91349746964a0edf4c0cdf091504f1887a2c1159f57",
      "fingerprint": "62f120370bd53e9938b878ca2501361274b74b73f0a2998dbe1941fa5398919f",
      "cached": true,
      "duration_seconds": 50.966,
      "sample_rate": 48000,
      "channels": 1,
      "integrated_lufs": -20.0,
      "true_peak_dbtp": -2.7,
      "leading_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "trailing_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "So what's happening in the brain?",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.866
        },
        {
          "text": "A 2026 review, by Vayga Zarza and colleagues, pulled together brain studies of attitude change driven by dissonance.",
          "start": 2.816,
          "end": 10.47
        },
        {
          "text": "And it points to two different jobs.",
          "start": 11.02,
          "end": 13.065
        },
        {
          "text": "First, noticing the conflict. That seems to involve the anterior sing-gyoo-lit cortex…",
          "start": 14.165,
          "end": 19.116
        },
        {
          "text": "a region that helps monitor conflict.",
          "start": 19.616,
          "end": 22.12
        },
        {
          "text": "Second, updating the attitude afterwards.",
          "start": 22.97,
          "end": 25.604
        },
        {
          "text": "That seems linked to the dorso-lateral prefrontal cortex.",
          "start": 26.104,
          "end": 29.64
        },
        {
          "text": "In other words, spotting a contradiction and resolving it…",
          "start": 30.64,
          "end": 33.895
        },
        {
          "text": "may not be the same step.",
          "start": 34.395,
          "end": 35.838
        },
        {
          "text": "But be careful with that.",
          "start": 36.788,
          "end": 38.322
        },
        {
          "text": "There's no single contradiction detector in your head.",
          "start": 38.652,
          "end": 41.823
        },
        {
          "text": "No brain scan can tell you whether someone is rationalising.",
          "start": 42.443,
          "end": 46.027
        },
        {
          "text": "These regions do many jobs…",
          "start": 46.407,
          "end": 48.097
        },
        {
          "text": "and the details are still being worked out.",
          "start": 48.597,
          "end": 50.949
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "s07-everyday",
      "asset_id": "narr-s07-everyday",
      "route": "tts",
      "path": "narration/s07-everyday/de0d63c573ebff93.wav",
      "sha256": "593e74e2c6912ee793ea48dc56d6dc57235af2a40d3a83d9bf5d015300e45499",
      "fingerprint": "de0d63c573ebff93dbe8656192c9f4d7881adbf034c5aca832117d10153760d2",
      "cached": true,
      "duration_seconds": 51.832,
      "sample_rate": 48000,
      "channels": 1,
      "integrated_lufs": -20.0,
      "true_peak_dbtp": -1.7,
      "leading_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "trailing_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "Now take this out of the lab.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 1.602
        },
        {
          "text": "You can spot these patterns in ordinary life.",
          "start": 2.022,
          "end": 4.659
        },
        {
          "text": "Not as labels for other people…",
          "start": 5.209,
          "end": 7.199
        },
        {
          "text": "but as things to look for in yourself.",
          "start": 7.699,
          "end": 9.871
        },
        {
          "text": "Someone misses a promotion. And decides promotions never really mattered.",
          "start": 10.821,
          "end": 15.349
        },
        {
          "text": "That could be honest reflection.",
          "start": 15.729,
          "end": 17.627
        },
        {
          "text": "Or a way to protect their self-esteem.",
          "start": 18.127,
          "end": 20.516
        },
        {
          "text": "Someone keeps pouring money into a failing project.",
          "start": 21.616,
          "end": 24.497
        },
        {
          "text": "Because quitting would make everything they've already spent feel wasted.",
          "start": 24.917,
          "end": 28.602
        },
        {
          "text": "Someone who sees themselves as honest tells a small lie.",
          "start": 29.452,
          "end": 32.667
        },
        {
          "text": "And decides the situation made it necessary.",
          "start": 32.997,
          "end": 35.813
        },
        {
          "text": "And sometimes, when a belief is challenged, we get more certain…",
          "start": 36.813,
          "end": 40.498
        },
        {
          "text": "instead of more curious.",
          "start": 40.998,
          "end": 42.384
        },
        {
          "text": "So here's the signal to watch for.",
          "start": 43.334,
          "end": 45.358
        },
        {
          "text": "The double standard. Are we asking more of the evidence against us…",
          "start": 45.808,
          "end": 49.746
        },
        {
          "text": "than the evidence for us?",
          "start": 50.246,
          "end": 51.812
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "s08-dangerous",
      "asset_id": "narr-s08-dangerous",
      "route": "tts",
      "path": "narration/s08-dangerous/94f426e6304a8093.wav",
      "sha256": "a53855ebf0add42c492c2ad9e370c44a77c1963142984cb286d55b75a74ea4b3",
      "fingerprint": "94f426e6304a809344376f52c07de0ccd58ea6e7dde527fefc8ff114222b3e1f",
      "cached": true,
      "duration_seconds": 56.354,
      "sample_rate": 48000,
      "channels": 1,
      "integrated_lufs": -20.1,
      "true_peak_dbtp": -1.9,
      "leading_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "trailing_silence_seconds": 0.0,
      "sentences": [
        {
          "text": "It's tempting to take all this as proof that people are irrational.",
          "start": 0.0,
          "end": 3.492
        },
        {
          "text": "But that misses the point.",
          "start": 3.912,
          "end": 5.194
        },
        {
          "text": "Beliefs organise our lives. They connect us to other people.",
          "start": 6.144,
          "end": 9.975
        },
        {
          "text": "So challenging one has real costs.",
          "start": 10.305,
          "end": 12.04
        },
        {
          "text": "And not every belief that survives criticism is a failure.",
          "start": 12.66,
          "end": 16.445
        },
        {
          "text": "Sometimes the evidence against it really is weak.",
          "start": 16.825,
          "end": 19.885
        },
        {
          "text": "The goal isn't to accept every contradiction.",
          "start": 20.985,
          "end": 23.878
        },
        {
          "text": "It's to tell the difference.",
          "start": 24.328,
          "end": 25.827
        },
        {
          "text": "A belief you hold because the evidence supports it…",
          "start": 26.247,
          "end": 29.112
        },
        {
          "text": "and a belief you hold because you've invested in defending it.",
          "start": 29.612,
          "end": 32.918
        },
        {
          "text": "That's hard to see from the inside.",
          "start": 33.768,
          "end": 35.533
        },
        {
          "text": "After all, a rationalisation rarely announces itself as one.",
          "start": 36.153,
          "end": 39.976
        },
        {
          "text": "It usually arrives dressed as an explanation.",
          "start": 40.356,
          "end": 43.198
        },
        {
          "text": "So ask yourself one thing.",
          "start": 44.198,
          "end": 45.491
        },
        {
          "text": "What evidence, specifically, would change my mind?",
          "start": 45.941,
          "end": 48.776
        },
        {
          "text": "If the honest answer is nothing…",
          "start": 49.346,
          "end": 51.27
        },
        {
          "text": "you may not be weighing a claim anymore.",
          "start": 51.77,
          "end": 53.979
        },
        {
          "text": "You may be protecting a commitment.",
          "start": 54.309,
          "end": 56.335
        }
      ],
      "warnings": []
    },
    {
      "scene_id": "s09-exercise",
      "asset_id": "narr-s09-exercise",
